ok><name>SUMIKAWA, NAOMI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HAMADA KAORU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KIMURA YOSHIHIDE</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MIDORIKAWA YOSHIMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SUMIKAWA NAOMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HAMADA, KAORU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KIMURA, YOSHIHIDE</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIDORIKAWA, YOSHIMI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUMIKAWA, NAOMI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A thermal recording material which has high sensitivity in color development and a high whiteness of the background and is excellent in image retention and heat resistance. The thermal recording material contains a dihydroxydiphenyl sulfone compound represented by general formula (I) as an organic color developer and 3-di-n-pentylamino-6-methyl-7-anilinofluoran as a colorless basic dye. (In the formula, R1 and R2 each represents C1-8 alkyl, alkenyl, or halogeno; and p and q each is an integer of 0 to 3.)</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>La présente invention concerne un matériau d'enregistrement thermique présentant une sensibilité élevée pour le développement couleurs, une bonne blancheur du fond, et de bonne qualités de tenue de l'image et de résistance à la chaleur. Ce matériau d'enregistrement thermique contient, d'une part un composé dihydroxydiphényle-sulfoné représenté par la formule générale (I) et intervenant comme développeur couleurs organique, et d'autre part une teinture basique incolore à base de 3-di-n-pentylamino-6-méthyle-7-anilinofluoran. Dans cette formule, R1 et R2 sont chacun C1-C8 alkyle, alcényle, ou halogène, et "p" et "q" sont chacun un entier de 0 à 3.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>